IMPORT prelude

-- Administration and Probate Act 1935 (Tas) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The Act counts its periods in months: "not earlier than 12 months before the date of his death" and
-- "not later than 6 months ... after the date of the grant" (s 27(5)(b)), "within 6 months after the termination of the
-- lease" (s 27(8)(a)), and "not less than one nor more than two [, two ... 4, 4 ... 8] months after the last of such
-- publications" (s 54(7)), and one period in years, "one year from the death" (s 43(1)).
-- A period of n months from a day ends on the corresponding day n months later (or earlier); where that month has no
-- corresponding day (31 August plus 6 months; 29 February plus 12 months), on the last day of that month (fork F7 in
-- NOTES.md).
--
-- (c) State of Tasmania. Quoted under CC BY 4.0 from an unofficial plain-text copy (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Based on
-- material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Administration and Probate Act 1935 (Tas)`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- Whether the first day is strictly before the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `falls before` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- The number of days in a month (1 to 12) of a year: from its first day to the first day of the next month.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 (y PLUS 1)) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 y)
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The corresponding day a whole number of months away (negative for earlier); if that month is too short, its last day.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the corresponding day` `n` `months from` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the month index` MEANS `the count` MODULO 12
        `the year` MEANS (`the count` MINUS `the month index`) DIVIDED BY 12
        `the month` MEANS `the month index` PLUS 1

-- n months after a day: the last day of a period of n months from it.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `n` `the day` MEANS `the corresponding day` `n` `months from` `the day`

-- n months before a day: the earliest day "not earlier than n months before" it.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months before` `n` `the day` MEANS `the corresponding day` (0 MINUS `n`) `months from` `the day`
